<p class="prose" style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-secondary);">Corrected figures are computed by removing Oman's share of each importer's Gulf-sourced nitrogenous fertiliser trade from the Hormuz-specific dependency total. Rounded to the nearest percentage point given the underlying commodity tier, see limitations below.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-label">Model limitations</div>
  <div class="callout-body">Nitrogenous fertiliser (HS 3102) is Tier 2, Corroborated, in the Narrows model, not Tier 1, Reported. Unlike crude oil and LNG, which have dedicated primary-source feeds behind them, this commodity is built from UN Comtrade bilateral pulls without an independent corroborating source layer. The dependency figures above should be read as directionally solid, not to the decimal point. The Oman correction itself is a routing fact, not a modelling assumption, Sur's geography relative to the strait is not in dispute, but the underlying trade values it is applied to carry the same estimation uncertainty as the rest of the model's fertiliser coverage.</div>
</div>

